          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "The work needed to bring a charge $q$ from infinity to a point is $W = qV$, where $V$ is the potential at that point.\nThe third corner is at a distance $r = 3\\ \\text{cm} = 0.03\\ \\text{m}$ from each of the two charges.\nThe potential at the third corner is $V = \\frac{1}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0}\\frac{(q_1+q_2)}{r} = \\frac{9\\times10^9 \\times (1+2)\\times10^{-9}}{0.03}\\ \\text{V}$.\nThis gives $V = \\frac{27}{0.03}\\ \\text{V} = 900\\ \\text{V}$.\nSo $W = qV = (3\\times10^{-9}\\ \\text{C})(900\\ \\text{V}) = 2.7\\times10^{-6}\\ \\text{J} = 2.7\\ \\mu\\text{J}$.\nAnswer: (C) 2.7"
